// Browser: no provider key anywhere.
async function askHelper(question) {
  const response = await fetch("/api/helper", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    credentials: "same-origin",                   // session cookie identifies the learner.
    body: JSON.stringify({ question }),
  });
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);
  return response.json();
}

// Server (sketch): reads the key from its own environment.
// POST /api/helper -> check session, rate-limit, then call the provider
// with process.env.AI_PROVIDER_KEY and return only the answer.
```

| Data | Where it belongs |
|---|---|
| provider/API secret keys. | server environment only. |
| session identity. | httpOnly, Secure cookie. |
| public IDs (e.g. a maps key restricted by domain). | may be in the client, with restrictions set by the provider. |
| personal data (email, birthday). | server, only if needed; not localStorage or logs. |

